<section class="sec" id="workflow">
<div class="hd2">
<div><div class="eyeb">The resubmission loop</div><h2>Four steps, one ledger.</h2></div>
<p class="sub">A rejected claim should not vanish into a queue. Bix forces a workflow on every denial: same data, same owner, same clock.</p>
</div>
<div class="flow">
<article class="step gl"><div class="no">01</div><h3>Submit</h3><p>Claim dispatched to the right payer portal with the right attachment and pre-auth reference.</p><div class="m">Median <b>4.2s</b> per claim</div></article>
<article class="step gl"><div class="no">02</div><h3>Adjudicate</h3><p>Remittance advice pulled and paired with the original claim. Matching is reconciled, not guessed.</p><div class="m">Match rate <b>99.4%</b></div></article>
<article class="step gl"><div class="no">03</div><h3>Detect</h3><p>Denials categorised by payer, code, clinician and facility the moment they land.</p><div class="m">Same-day <b>100%</b></div></article>
<article class="step gl"><div class="no">04</div><h3>Resubmit</h3><p>Each rejection lands in a tracked workflow with owner, SLA and reason — nothing sits unseen.</p><div class="m">Avg. close <b>1d 04h</b></div></article>
</div>
</section>

